1
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:24,750
Vibrant and Whimsical!

2
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:43,500
One Man Band is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Mark Andrews.

3
00:00:56,250 --> 00:01:02,250
With one coin to make a wish at the piazza fountain, a peasant girl encounters two competing
street performers who'd prefer the coin find its way into their tip jars.

4
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The little girl, Tippy, is caught in the middle as a
musical duel ensues between the one-man-bands.

5
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:39,750
One Man Band is a 2005 Pixar animated musical comedy short film.

6
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:58,500
It debuted at the 29th Annecy International Animated Film Festival in Annecy, France, and
won the Platinum Grand Prize at the Future Film Festival in Bologna, Italy.

7
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:17,250
It was shown with the theatrical release of Cars.

8
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
It was written and directed by Andrew Jimenez and Mark Andrews and
produced by Osnat Shurer, head of Pixar's Shorts group.

9
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:54,750
The score was composed by Michael Giacchino.

10
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:13,500
Like many Pixar shorts, it is completely free of dialogue and vocal effects, instead
using music (played by the characters) and pantomime to tell the story.

11
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:32,250
Unlike most Pixar shorts, which are driven solely by storyboarding and scriptwriting, the music in One Man Band was developed
alongside the film's story; Giacchino collaborated extensively with the film's directors due to the music's large role.

12
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:51,000
On January 31, 2006, it was nominated for the Academy
Award for Best Animated Short Film.

13
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:09,750
It was included in the Animation Show of Shows in 2005.

14
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:28,500
The film explores themes of fountain, rivalry, coin, bag of money, little girl.

15
00:04:41,250 --> 00:04:47,250
The tone is lighthearted.
